# libgudev -- GObject bindings for libudev.
#
# The GNOME stack does not call libudev directly. upower enumerates batteries
# through GUdev, gnome-settings-daemon watches input and backlight devices
# through it, and gnome-control-center's device panels read it. It is a thin
# wrapper and it is on the required path of everything that has to know what
# hardware is present.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/libgudev/238/libgudev-238.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=61266ab1afc9d73dbc60a8b2af73e99d2fdff47d99544d085760e4fa667b5dd1
SRC_DIR=libgudev-238

# THE ONE THING THAT COULD FAIL HERE, AND IT IS A VERSION FLOOR WITH NO
# HEADROOM. meson.build asks for
#
#     libudev_req = '>= 251'
#     libudev_dep = dependency('libudev', version: libudev_req)
#
# and this distribution's libudev comes from eudev 3.2.14, whose libudev.pc
# declares `Version: 251` -- eudev tracks systemd's interface number rather than
# its own release number. Measured against the installed .pc rather than assumed
# from the package version, because eudev 3.2.14 and libudev 251 look like
# unrelated numbers and the first reading of them is that this cannot work.
#
# If eudev is ever replaced or its .pc version drops, this stops at configure
# with a version mismatch rather than silently building a libgudev against
# something older -- which is the good direction, and the reason for recording
# it here rather than being surprised by it.
#
# -Dintrospection=enabled. Upstream default is 'auto', and gobject-introspection
# IS packaged -- so auto resolves to the right answer today, by accident. Named
# so the answer stays right the day something reorders the build: a libgudev
# without its typelib builds, installs and links, and the failure appears in
# whatever JavaScript or Python later asks for GUdev-1.0.
#
# -Dvapi=disabled. Also 'auto'; vala is not packaged, so auto resolves off
# today. meson.build asserts that vapi implies introspection, so this is the
# arm of that pair that cannot be left to chance if vala ever arrives.
#
# -Dtests=disabled. 'auto', and it needs umockdev, which is not packaged. With
# it left at auto the tests are silently skipped; disabling it says so.
#
# -Dgtk_doc is false by default and needs gtk-doc, which is not packaged.
MESON_ARGS="-Dintrospection=enabled -Dvapi=disabled -Dtests=disabled"
